---
layout: base.njk
title: "Work"
description: "Selected work by Waseem Ilyas. A few projects where the mix mattered more than any single skill. Some public, some anonymised."
permalink: "/work/"
---
<section class="console section" aria-label="Selected work">
  <span class="reg tl" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="reg tr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-head" data-cal="0">
      <span class="ref">WORK</span>
      <h1>Selected work</h1>
      <p>A few projects where the mix mattered more than any single skill. Some are public. Some are anonymised to protect client privacy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="worklist" data-cal="1">
      {#- Each row shows the case's role, craft and outcome from its own datasheet,
          so a reader can compare the work before opening any of it. The title is
          the link and stretches over the row (as on Notes), so its name stays short. #}
      {%- for cs in collections.casestudies %}
      <article class="workcard workcard-spec">
        <span class="ref">{{ cs.data.ref }}</span>
        <div>
          <h2><a href="{{ cs.url }}" data-prefetch-article>{{ cs.data.title }}</a></h2>
          <span class="kick">{{ cs.data.kicker }}</span>
          <dl class="workspec">
            {%- for row in cs.data.datasheet %}{% if row.k in ["ROLE", "CRAFT", "OUTCOME"] %}
            <div><dt>{{ row.k | lower | capitalize }}</dt><dd>{{ row.v | replace(" · ", "&nbsp;· ") | safe }}</dd></div>
            {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
          </dl>
        </div>
        <span class="go" aria-hidden="true">Read →</span>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
